  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P align=justify>Our new Canadian Staff member Sonny sent us some photographs he took at the "Revolver" premiere in Toronto he attended with his friend Frank. He also sent us a story of the event.</P>
<P align=justify>"<STRONG>Frank</STRONG> and <STRONG>I</STRONG>, received <STRONG>Gala Priority Tickets</STRONG> to go to the World Premier of <STRONG>Revolver</STRONG> - A <STRONG>Guy Ritichie</STRONG> Movie. When entering the <STRONG>Roy Thomson Hall</STRONG>, we were very excited. We wanted to go in as soon as possible so we can get our first pick of seats (first come first serve in seat selection).<BR><BR>We were seated in L6, which <STRONG>Mr. and Mrs. Ritchie</STRONG> were seated in section L5. At first we sat down and thought that these seats were terrible on he balcony and no view of any one famous let alone <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG> and <STRONG>Guy</STRONG>. <BR><BR>So at one point a lady next to us said she just saw the couple entering the building, we of course were so excited, and still at this point have no clue what was to come. <BR><BR>Our eyes were wondering trying to figure out where they would be seated. At one point, I looked to our right and noticed that a section of seats were reserved. <BR><BR>As I continue to examine those seats, <STRONG>Frank</STRONG> and <STRONG>I</STRONG> both noticed, and both read out loud, <STRONG>Reserved Guy Ritchie</STRONG>, <STRONG>Mrs. Ritchie</STRONG>, <STRONG>Ray Liotta</STRONG>... HOLLY CRAP, she is seated 5 seats to our right in the same row. Our hearts started to beat faster than a speeding bullet. <BR><BR>As the show began, <STRONG>Guy</STRONG> was introducing the movie and all the actors. When he left the stage, a few moments later, here she comes escorted down the the aisle by the ushers with small flash lights making sure she is careful walking down the stairs. <BR><BR>Then there she was, as beautiful as a rose, as perfect as a butterfly. She was magnificent….an aura that I cannot explain. <BR><BR>People ask me, so how was the movie. My reply, and probably <STRONG>Frank</STRONG>'s, was hard to follow, when she is seated next to you… <BR>But, <STRONG>I also did enjoy the movie</STRONG>…WAY TO GUY…" </P>
<P align=center><A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/01.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/01_small.jpg" border=0></A>&nbsp;<A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/01.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/02_small.jpg" border=0></A></P>
<P align=center><A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/03.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/03_small.jpg" border=0></A>&nbsp;<A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/04.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/04_small.jpg" border=0></A></P>
<P align=center><A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/05.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/05_small.jpg" border=0></A>&nbsp;<A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/06.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/06_small.jpg" border=0></A></P>
<P align=center><A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/07.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/07_small.jpg" border=0></A>&nbsp;<A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/08.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/08_small.jpg" border=0></A>&nbsp;<A href="/images/2005/canada/revolver/09.jpg" target=_blank><IMG src="/images/2005/canada/revolver/09_small.jpg" border=0></A></P><img src="/corrispondenti/co-sonny_canada.jpg" border="0">
</font></div>
